# Three attacks per second (O426, owner 2026-11-06: "raise the attack limit to 3 per second. Make it reachable too, but
# balanced"; server/README.md "Attack speed cap"). Moves two defaults of patch 0011, nothing else in C++:
#  1. minPlayerAttackInterval 1000 -> 333: no player swings faster than 3 times per second (the hard floor of every source
#     together: vocation, weapon modifier, gems, dexterity, the passive tree, worn pieces).
#  2. maxPlayerAttackSpeedBonus 40 -> 76: all bonuses together shorten the vocation-scaled interval by at most 76%. A min-
#     maxed build (weapon 30, dexterity 20, tree + worn pieces 45) cuts 75.5%: Shadowfist 1300 -> 333 (the floor), Ninja
#     1400 -> 343, a 2000 ms class 2000 -> 490.
# The leech rule (minPlayerLeechInterval = 900) is untouched: leech still heals at most once per 900 ms. The damage per hit
# of a fast swing is cut in Lua (data/scripts/chaos/attack_rate_core.lua, weapon_styles.lua), so no engine damage code.
# config.lua keys of the same names still win; a server that names them keeps its own numbers.
# Lua mirror: ChaosItemMods.attackCap (data/lib/chaos_item_mods.lua), tests/attack_speed_cap_test.lua reads this file.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0087: patch -p1 < 0088-attack-speed-3-per-second.patch, then rebuild (not
# compiled here: the base tree is not in git; dry-run checked on the configmanager.cpp lines of 0011 and 0015).
--- a/src/configmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/configmanager.cpp
@@ -299,4 +299,4 @@ bool ConfigManager::load()
 	// minPlayerLeechInterval ms each (0 turns a rule off)
-	integer[MIN_PLAYER_ATTACK_INTERVAL] = getGlobalNumber(L, "minPlayerAttackInterval", 1000);
-	integer[MAX_PLAYER_ATTACK_SPEED_BONUS] = getGlobalNumber(L, "maxPlayerAttackSpeedBonus", 40);
+	integer[MIN_PLAYER_ATTACK_INTERVAL] = getGlobalNumber(L, "minPlayerAttackInterval", 333); // Chaos (patch 0088): 3 attacks per second
+	integer[MAX_PLAYER_ATTACK_SPEED_BONUS] = getGlobalNumber(L, "maxPlayerAttackSpeedBonus", 76);
 	integer[MIN_PLAYER_LEECH_INTERVAL] = getGlobalNumber(L, "minPlayerLeechInterval", 900);
